3. ROYALTY ON SALE

Where the Software, or a derivative of it, is sold, resold, sublicensed for a fee, bundled into a paid product or
service, or otherwise commercially distributed to any entity, a royalty is owed to the copyright holder.

  3.1  The royalty is up to twenty percent (20%) of the gross amount received for the Software, or for the paid
       product or service in which it is a material component, per transaction.

  3.2  Twenty percent (20%) applies unless the copyright holder agrees a lower rate in writing. Any agreed reduction
       applies only to the specific arrangement and period named in that writing.

  3.3  Where a fee is charged on a recurring basis (subscription, retainer, hosted access), the royalty is calculated
       on each period's gross receipt for so long as the Software remains a material component.

  3.4  Royalty is payable in the same currency as the sale, within thirty (30) days of receipt, or of the close of
       the period for recurring fees.

  3.5  The seller must, on request and no more often than quarterly, provide a written statement of the sales on
       which royalty was calculated. Records sufficient to verify the statement are to be kept for three (3) years.

